    "rationale": "Chosen dataset: coco2017_det_train as the sole training source for all three classes (person, dog, cat). Rationale: - coco2017_det_train is a well-established, unified training source that provides annotation-consistent data across all three target classes, enabling a cohesive backbone and straightforward per-class sampling. - This satisfies the maximum_generalization_sources constraint (1) by using a single primary pool. - Target per-class pool is 2250 images, and coco2017_det_train has ample training samples for each class (person: 64115, dog: 4385, cat: 4114), allowing 2250 images per class without exceeding availability. - Using one primary dataset supports domain alignment considerations and reduces leakage risk, while facilitating consistent annotation semantics across classes. - Per-class totals: 2250 person + 2250 dog + 2250 cat = 6750 images in the primary pool. There may be overlaps (the same image containing multiple target classes) which would reduce the unique image count in practice, but the per-class quotas are satisfied. Approximate total download allocation: 6750 images from coco2017_det_train. Budget: no explicit download budget constraint triggered, as per-class quotas are within available counts and the single-source choice aligns with the policy.",
